____________________________________________________________________________________________________
FINAL STEADY STATE (no absorbing barrier)
____________________________________________________________________________________________________

J N = R F without a barrier: under continuous formation, after the stabilized population has reached its own
steady state, the yields of every exit, chemical activation and thermal reaction together (GO10 eqs. 7-9).

Not available: T = 300 K, p = 7500.616827041697 Torr: relative residual 4.004465538441496e-8 of J N = F exceeds the tolerance 1e-8. In the final steady state this means that J is numerically singular: the thermal rate coefficient of a well without a bimolecular sink is negligible compared with the collision frequency (the final steady state is reached only after about 0.1/k_uni, O02 text after eq. 13); use the intermediate steady state for such conditions.
Not available: T = 300 K, p = 75006.16827041698 Torr: relative residual 3.547966344686523e-7 of J N = F exceeds the tolerance 1e-8. In the final steady state this means that J is numerically singular: the thermal rate coefficient of a well without a bimolecular sink is negligible compared with the collision frequency (the final steady state is reached only after about 0.1/k_uni, O02 text after eq. 13); use the intermediate steady state for such conditions.
